Day 25
----------

xpath axes
----------


* Self: `self` means selecting the current element itself.
* Parent: `parent` means moving one level up to the immediate parent element.
* Child: `child` means moving one level down to the immediate child element.
* Ancestor: `ancestor` means moving up through all parent levels.
* Descendant: `descendant` means moving down through all child levels.
* Following: `following` means selecting elements that come after the current element anywhere in the page.
* Preceding: `preceding` means selecting elements that come **before the current element anywhere in the page.
* Following-sibling: `following-sibling` means selecting an element that comes after the current element with the same parent.
* Preceding-sibling: `preceding-sibling` means selecting an element that comes before the current element with the same parent.
